WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.528
- [Voiceover] This is me suffering

00:00:01.528 --> 00:00:04.695
from another anxiety attack in Dallas,

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.259
24 hours after bullet casings

00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:09.783
were picked up from the streets,

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:11.459
I went to Dallas.

00:00:11.459 --> 00:00:12.688
24 hours before that,

00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:15.735
I was at a black lives matter protest.

00:00:15.735 --> 00:00:17.532
If you were to ask me how Dallas was,

00:00:17.532 --> 00:00:19.573
I could not deliver a quick summary,

00:00:19.573 --> 00:00:21.803
but I can tell you all the things

00:00:21.803 --> 00:00:22.872
that ran through my mind,

00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:25.199
because they haven't left me.

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:27.955
Instead of visiting
Dallas to go see museums

00:00:27.955 --> 00:00:29.924
and eat barbecue,

00:00:29.924 --> 00:00:32.073
my hotel sat right across the street

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:35.113
from where the shooting took place.

00:00:35.113 --> 00:00:35.946
I couldn't eat,

00:00:35.946 --> 00:00:37.092
and I couldn't sleep,

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:39.892
so I just did what I do best,

00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:41.225
and that's film.

00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:47.448
Children, some who didn't understand,

00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:52.204
and unfortunately some who did,

00:00:52.204 --> 00:00:54.412
and it was not about a city divided,

00:00:54.412 --> 00:00:56.598
but a city that came together in mourning,

00:00:56.598 --> 00:01:00.181
and now their lives
are stricken with fear.

00:01:01.889 --> 00:01:04.994
I thought about how many
anxiety attacks I had

00:01:04.994 --> 00:01:05.994
in one week.

00:01:07.246 --> 00:01:08.163
It was six.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:10.958
I couldn't breathe,

00:01:10.958 --> 00:01:13.875
and all I wanted to do was breathe.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:16.791
- I thank you for the love.

00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:18.829
You know, love travels a long ways.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:20.255
- [Voiceover] And, I met a homeless woman,

00:01:20.255 --> 00:01:23.515
and I thought about the
last time I had cried,

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.783
so I cried with her.

00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:27.476
- Thank you.

00:01:27.476 --> 00:01:29.119
- Just coming together as a community,

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:30.640
that's what we really need to do.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.807
- [Voiceover] My Uber drivers
became taxi cab confessionals.

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:40.700
Some revealing how they were
in the midst of the tragedy.

00:01:44.448 --> 00:01:48.423
I didn't want to remember
Dallas for its tragedy,

00:01:48.423 --> 00:01:49.994
but even as I tried to leave Dallas,

00:01:49.994 --> 00:01:54.161
the security level was so high
that it was hard to leave,

00:01:56.014 --> 00:01:56.847
and even as I did,

00:01:56.847 --> 00:01:57.995
all I could think about were the people

00:01:57.995 --> 00:02:01.386
that were left behind with pain.

00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:03.412
When I got to the airport
I looked up to the news

00:02:03.412 --> 00:02:05.704
and saw that there was
shooting in Michigan

00:02:05.704 --> 00:02:07.913
not too far from my grandfather,

00:02:07.913 --> 00:02:09.647
and it made me think,

00:02:09.647 --> 00:02:12.611
in the midst of tragedies like Orlando,

00:02:12.611 --> 00:02:15.858
Baton Rouge, Minnesota, and now Dallas,

00:02:15.858 --> 00:02:18.858
where was I going to travel to next?

00:02:22.503 --> 00:02:25.170
(upbeat music)

